course: dictionary
lesson: 14415
title: Overlapping
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When two things overlap, part of one lies over part of the other, so they share a patch. Think of two sheets of paper: if one sits partly on top of the other, the two sheets are overlapping. «The two circles on the board are overlapping.» The clue is that the circles touch, and the shared patch in the middle belongs to both.
explain: Overlapping can also be about time. «Our swimming lesson and the football match have overlapping times.» If both start at four o'clock, some of each one happens at the same moment. Look for clue words like both, same and share. Ask yourself: is some of one thing happening inside the other?
explain: This word is the -ing form of the verb overlap. You may also see overlaps and overlapped. «The tiles on the roof are overlapping, so the rain runs off and stays out.» Each tile covers part of the tile below it, and that is what keeps the water out.
fact: Overlapping means covering part of something else, so two things lie partly over each other.
fact: Overlapping ideas or times share some part in common.
fact: «Overlapping circles» in a Venn diagram show things that belong to both groups; the overlap is the middle part.
fact: Fish scales and roof tiles are overlapping to keep water out.
fact: Overlap is the verb: overlap, overlaps, overlapped, overlapping.
exercise: «The two circles are overlapping.» What does the middle part show? | The colour of the paper | Things that belong to neither group | *Things that belong to both groups | The size of the board
exercise: «Our lessons have overlapping times.» What does overlapping times mean? | Both lessons are cancelled | The clock is broken | The lessons are never at the same time | *Some of the time is shared at the same moment
exercise: «The tiles on the roof are overlapping.» Why are they overlapping? | To hide the chimney | To make the roof heavier | To change colour in the sun | *To keep water out
test: «The two photos are overlapping on the table.» What does this mean? | Lying far apart from each other | *Lying partly over each other | Stacked up in a tall tower | Hidden inside a box
test: Which word is the verb that overlapping comes from? | overlook | overtake | outline | *overlap
exam: «The two meetings have overlapping times, so Priya can only go to one.» What does this tell us? | There are no meetings today | *Some of the two meetings' times are at the same moment | The meetings are in the same room | Priya will go to both meetings, one after the other
